{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/21677-dragonblooded-breeding-and-the-scarlet-empress","id":21677,"title":"Dragonblooded Breeding and the Scarlet Empress","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-02T09:06:44-08:00","id":21677,"title":"Dragonblooded Breeding and the Scarlet Empress","content":"I've got something that confuses me, sort of a logical hiccup I've noticed. I was wondering if it could be clarified? Maybe in the Dragonblooded book when it comes out? (If the same issue arises despite the canon-change.)<br /> <br /> So the problem arises from this:<br /> <br /> 1. Dragonblooded houses tend to be one caste, so much so that &quot;off-caste&quot; children are shunned a bit. (Still better than not Exalting. I always imagine it's like the family who wanted you to graduate from College as a Doctor, when you graduate in Fine Arts. Unexalting is like flunking out of college. <i>Some</i> families are happy if you graduate at all...)<br /> <br /> 2. The major houses trace their lineage to the Scarlet Empress.<br /> <br /> 3. The Scarlet Empress is Earth Aspect.<br /> <br /> 4. Aspects are lineage-dependent. Mostly.<br /> <br /> With all of this, shouldn't that mean that there should be a higher probability of Earth aspects in ALL of the households? Particularly the younger households, like V'neef?<br /> <br /> Unless....maybe the Empress actually has an <i>abysmal</i> breeding score, so that her aspect is almost completely overpowered by her partners?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T09:21:45-08:00","id":21689,"title":"","content":"I believe that Transcendent Gaian Harmony was supposed to justify this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T09:22:58-08:00","id":21692,"title":"","content":"I believe the idea that purity of Aspect was a big deal was an addition in Second Edition, and it was probably ill-considered for all reasons including the ones that you point out.<br /> <br /> Still, even within the likelihood of hereditary Aspect, the Empress has had a lot of children, and only a relative minority of them are at the top of Great Houses. There's placement enough for those who don't inherit her Aspect to be disproportionately represented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T09:27:06-08:00","id":21694,"title":"","content":"Purity of Aspect is kind of junk for reasons Isator mentioned. I personally ignore it for the most part. My DB have a 60% chance to exalt as their house aspect, with a 10% chance of each other. I have a chart I use for randomizing NPC's when needed that uses those calculations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/695-kenshin138","name":"kenshin138","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T09:30:33-08:00","id":21698,"title":"","content":"I guess Sidereal shenanigans could also explain it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T09:32:21-08:00","id":21700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/21677-dragonblooded-breeding-and-the-scarlet-empress#post21677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. The Scarlet Empress is Earth Aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>She devoured her siblings and gained some of their elemental affinity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T09:35:15-08:00","id":21703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/21677-dragonblooded-breeding-and-the-scarlet-empress?p=21692#post21692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the idea that purity of Aspect was a big deal was an addition in Second Edition, and it was probably ill-considered for all reasons including the ones that you point out.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bEven in Second Addition, purity of Aspect is just something that the Dragonbloods believed. In MoEP: DBs (p29) it outright says that the Sidereals know its BS, they just don't feel like telling the Scarlet Dynasty.<br /> <br /> Also, we don't know were her partners are coming from. I image that a large number of them (at least early on) were prominent members of Shogunate Gens' whose breeding were at least equal to her own. So if the aspect tracks based off the stronger breeding parent, what happens if they're both the same?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T10:15:43-08:00","id":21746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/21677-dragonblooded-breeding-and-the-scarlet-empress?p=21703#post21703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bEven in Second Addition, purity of Aspect is just something that the Dragonbloods believed. In MoEP: DBs (p29) it outright says that the Sidereals know its BS, they just don't feel like telling the Scarlet Dynasty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. That's pretty mind blowingly stupid. I mean, the Exaltation is basically the most important thing, period, full stop, to the Dynasty. While I can certainly imagine a range of supersticions and prejudices around Aspect, lineage and breeding- especially amongst the patricians -I'd expect the the sages and savants of the Scarlet Dynasty to have a pretty good handle on most of what is and isn't BS in pure, practical terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T10:21:58-08:00","id":21754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/21677-dragonblooded-breeding-and-the-scarlet-empress?p=21692#post21692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the idea that purity of Aspect was a big deal was an addition in Second Edition, and it was probably ill-considered for all reasons including the ones that you point out.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was Cathak Canian's psychopathic father back in 1e who was treating his (other) son Exalting as a Water Aspected as definitive proof that he had been cuckolded and nearly killed his wife over it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T11:14:39-08:00","id":21777,"title":"","content":"There's also that the Empress wasn't really a terribly important sort before her group took over the Manse and she became empress. Another element of her having had high breeding that is weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T11:16:29-08:00","id":21779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dulahan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/21677-dragonblooded-breeding-and-the-scarlet-empress?p=21777#post21777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also that the Empress wasn't really a terribly important sort before her group took over the Manse and she became empress. Another element of her having had high breeding that is weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lot of people had high Breeding in the Shogunate. More than now, at least. Blood of Dragons has thinned and all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Once, there was a maiden... who spent all her time on the internet.<br /> &quot;Someone out there is WRONG,&quot; she said.<br /> So she tossed a noose made of golden light... and strangled her opponent.<br /> Both of them died alone.<br /> &quot;Love is for football players and cheerleaders,&quot; her obituary said.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","name":"notthepenguins","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"359"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T12:03:41-08:00","id":21811,"title":"","content":"Ok, fun facts time.<br /> <br /> Empress's Children:<br /> <br /> 1. Manosque aspect unknown<br /> 2. Ragara Earth aspect, father Rawar<br /> 3. Sesus Fire aspect, mortal father<br /> 4. Ledaal Air aspect, mortal father<br /> 5. Mnemon Earth aspect, father Rawar<br /> 6. Cynis, problematic, probably Wood aspect<br /> 7. V'Neef Water aspect, father was of &quot;purest&quot; breeding<br /> 8. Lillun, mortal<br /> <br /> So there you go. Assuming Cynis is wood aspect (not a big ask, but Second Edition changed Cynis's <i>gender</i> as well as his/her founding of the Red Piss Legion), then the Empress has twice as many children of her (&quot;real&quot;) aspect as she has of her &quot;off&quot; aspects (taken individually, that is). At least one of those &quot;off-aspects&quot; comes from the Dragonblooded male with the best breeding score she could find in all Creation. Two of those off aspects come as a result of sullying her womb with mortal seed.<br /> <br /> Also doesn't carrying a child to term in a manse make the child that aspect (or is that superstition)? Between Gaian Harmony and being able to walk into any manse on the Blessed Isle, I don't see a problem with the Empress having whatever breed of child she wants.<br /> <br /> Five of the Great Houses aren't even founded by her children (like Tepet, for example, which was founded by her consort... Tepet, or Nellens which was founded by her consort Nellens' patrician children).<br /> <br /> [edit]<br /> <br /> inb4 &quot;The Seed is Strong.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-02-2013, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T15:48:35-08:00","id":21938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notthepenguins</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dulahan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also that the Empress wasn't really a terribly important sort before her group took over the Manse and she became empress. Another element of her having had high breeding that is weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lot of people had high Breeding in the Shogunate. More than now, at least. Blood of Dragons has thinned and all.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the possibility that, in an environment in which there are so much more of them, the prestige of high Breeding is a lot less acute. The Empress has always been said to have come from a good background; that this didn't automatically equate to her being highly ranked or widely known can tell us some things about the Shogunate.<br /> <br /> Really, when there are so many of them, having as many Exalted children as possible might not be so big a deal. And in spite of (or depending on the historical period you're drawing parallels with, concurrent to) the use of titles like daimyo, something about the indications of Dragon Blooded in Records of the Before feel somewhat less... aristocratic than the Scarlet Dynasty does.<br /> <br /> Like, not to a huge degree, but the texture might be a bit smoother.<br /> <br /> Point is, who had the best breeding probably wasn't as big of a deal before there were only a few thousand of them (and that's not so much in terms of &quot;we've got to keep the Terrestrial bloodline from dying out!&quot; as it was and is &quot;we've got to maximize the power of our family so we have the best odds of asserting our claims in this suddenly small pond&quot;).<br /> <br /> That's another thing; having slightly more Exalted family members might not have been as important as having a few personal warstriders, or private golem army, or a little fleet of flying machines bunkered up on your property.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T15:56:41-08:00","id":21946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/21677-dragonblooded-breeding-and-the-scarlet-empress?p=21811#post21811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">sullying her womb with mortal seed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nellens may have been mortal, but I don't think there's any particular indication that he didn't have Terrestrial lineage, and it seems more likely on several counts that he did.<br /> <br /> I'm very happy at the implication that a Breeding Merit will be available to mortals (and possibly other Exalted) now.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd like it if the language was less built on terms of whether or not the person you're having a child with is mortal and more around the idea of being descended from the right people. Actually using the word &quot;ancestor&quot; a bit more often wouldn't necessarily go amiss either.<br /> <br /> Like, being Exalted certainly <i>matters</i>, but it really matters mostly as contributing to the statistics they can cite to show that this is a good bloodline, since that's really all they have to go off of. Really, Exalting doesn't just help <i>your</i> marriage prospects, it also makes your mortal siblings and nephews and nieces more eligible, since you're part of the numbers your family can point at and say &quot;see, their breeding is good, it's just that the Dragons passed them by&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T15:58:43-08:00","id":21950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/21677-dragonblooded-breeding-and-the-scarlet-empress?p=21754#post21754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was Cathak Canian's psychopathic father back in 1e who was treating his (other) son Exalting as a Water Aspected as definitive proof that he had been cuckolded and nearly killed his wife over it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, when your sociopathy takes that particular form, you can cite the shape of a child's nose as being proof that your wife cheated, and it holds as much water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T16:02:27-08:00","id":21954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/21677-dragonblooded-breeding-and-the-scarlet-empress?p=21946#post21946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nellens may have been mortal, but I don't think there's any particular indication that he didn't have Terrestrial lineage, and it seems more likely on several counts that he did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't one of the books specifically say that Nellens was a Patrician? Don't remember which one, but I could've sworn I read that somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T17:50:46-08:00","id":22013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/21677-dragonblooded-breeding-and-the-scarlet-empress?p=21811#post21811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, fun facts time.<br /> <br /> Empress's Children:<br /> <br /> 1. Manosque aspect unknown<br /> 2. Ragara Earth aspect, father Rawar<br /> 3. Sesus Fire aspect, mortal father<br /> 4. Ledaal Air aspect, mortal father<br /> 5. Mnemon Earth aspect, father Rawar<br /> 6. Cynis, problematic, probably Wood aspect<br /> 7. V'Neef Water aspect, father was of &quot;purest&quot; breeding<br /> 8. Lillun, mortal<br /> <br /> So there you go. Assuming Cynis is wood aspect (not a big ask, but Second Edition changed Cynis's <i>gender</i> as well as his/her founding of the Red Piss Legion), then the Empress has twice as many children of her (&quot;real&quot;) aspect as she has of her &quot;off&quot; aspects (taken individually, that is). At least one of those &quot;off-aspects&quot; comes from the Dragonblooded male with the best breeding score she could find in all Creation. Two of those off aspects come as a result of sullying her womb with mortal seed.<br /> <br /> Also doesn't carrying a child to term in a manse make the child that aspect (or is that superstition)? Between Gaian Harmony and being able to walk into any manse on the Blessed Isle, I don't see a problem with the Empress having whatever breed of child she wants.<br /> <br /> Five of the Great Houses aren't even founded by her children (like Tepet, for example, which was founded by her consort... Tepet, or Nellens which was founded by her consort Nellens' patrician children).<br /> <br /> [edit]<br /> <br /> inb4 &quot;The Seed is Strong.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does it say they had mortal fathers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1174-the-lidless-eye-that-sees","name":"The Lidless Eye That Sees","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1174_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T18:20:35-08:00","id":22036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/21677-dragonblooded-breeding-and-the-scarlet-empress?p=21950#post21950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, when your sociopathy takes that particular form, you can cite the shape of a child's nose as being proof that your wife cheated, and it holds as much water.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the problem was that Cathak Cainan did not highlight or provide context for how unusual that situation was. Your typical Dragon-Blooded marriage is a political alliance that meets up every few years to produce a child who belongs to the mother's house but Cainan's father is acting like a stereotypical medieval nobleman.<br /> <br /> Naturally we can always apply Occam's Razor and say whoever wrote that didn't know enough about Realm culture, but &quot;maybe the author was clueless?&quot; kind of kills fluff discussions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 12-02-2013, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T21:47:04-08:00","id":22114,"title":"","content":"Probably not the most important thing in the long run, but Peleps was another of the children of the Empress. Somehow 2e forgot to mention this.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Lidless Eye That Sees</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/21677-dragonblooded-breeding-and-the-scarlet-empress?p=22013#post22013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where does it say they had mortal fathers?</div> </div> </div> </div>The 1e core says Ledaal and Sesus were the children of Nellens, on page 41.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/103-gsd","name":"GSD","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T01:06:31-08:00","id":22189,"title":"","content":"It bears noting, I think, that the vast majority of current day Dynasts are several generations removed from Her Redness. That is plenty of time for other elements to take hold even if her children were all earth aspects instead of taking after their father's element or having a different element then either parent because of a fluke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T03:06:20-08:00","id":22222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 7. V'Neef Water aspect, father was of &quot;purest&quot; breeding </div> </div> </div>V\u2019neef is strongly wood aspected with legendary breeding actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/554-wwwhite","name":"wwwhite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar554_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T03:30:32-08:00","id":22228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/21677-dragonblooded-breeding-and-the-scarlet-empress?p=22036#post22036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the problem was that Cathak Cainan did not highlight or provide context for how unusual that situation was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having just reread the passage in question, I note two things:<br /> 1) Cainan notes that it's the <i>only</i> time he ever saw such a thing happen between them, and how it was terrifying (implying a degree of unfamiliarity).<br /> 2) Cainan uses the word &quot;combat&quot;, which implies that it was more of a duel, even if it was getting out of hand enough that intervention was necessary for one to not be killed (and the intervention itself implies that Cainan's father did not have latitude to go killing his wife).<br /> <br /> Not <i>quite</i> the stereotypical medieval nobleman, or even abusive asshole who reaches for excuses to engage in physical violence, I think.<br /> <br /> I mean, Exalted: The Dragon Blooded <i>does</i> include details about how becoming pregnant by somebody other than your husband is stigmatized (if Dynastic marriage is a business partnership, than having another man's child violates the terms of that partnership). The rest just seems kind of like Jukashi's idea of Exalted being more physically resilient means that arguments might escalate quickly. Cainan's mother is a Fire Aspect as well, she's probably just as inclined towards... let's call it passionate excess.<br /> <br /> The possibility that they had four more children together after that might imply that there weren't really hard feelings over it.<br /> <br /> If anything, I see it as even more of an insight into Dynast society, and it seems to fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T05:36:46-08:00","id":22289,"title":"","content":"It's clear the Empress is really just a sub soul of Gaia. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T06:21:53-08:00","id":22300,"title":"","content":"Couple things:<br /> <br /> 1) The Empress's Aspect wasn't set until <i>Return to the Scarlet Empress.</i> I know for a fact that it wasn't &quot;Earth, secretly, until RttSE revealed the truth to the world!&quot; because I've spoken to the person who wrote it. Notably, Grabowski always replied with &quot;Does she even have one anymore?&quot; when asked the Empress's aspect, so for the Earth thing, as with everything in RotSE, take it with a grain of salt.<br /> <br /> 2) There's a bit in Aspect Book: Air that suggests some bored secret society in the Shogunate aristocracy was engaged in a large-scale game of what's essentially sociopolitical <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nomic\" target=\"_blank\">Nomic</a> (see &quot;From a report by Magistrate-Captain Riarda Rikvashta,&quot; beginning page 63), and an offshoot of that involved a Dragon-Blooded breeding project. The hints are the Empress is one of the outputs of that. So there's a reason for her unusually strong bloodline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T07:09:22-08:00","id":22314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/21677-dragonblooded-breeding-and-the-scarlet-empress?p=22300#post22300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2) There's a bit in Aspect Book: Air that suggests some bored secret society in the Shogunate aristocracy was engaged in a large-scale game of what's essentially sociopolitical <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nomic\" target=\"_blank\">Nomic</a> (see &quot;From a report by Magistrate-Captain Riarda Rikvashta,&quot; beginning page 63), and an offshoot of that involved a Dragon-Blooded breeding project. The hints are the Empress is one of the outputs of that. So there's a reason for her unusually strong bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, this is where you find problems in having just <i>too many</i> good things in a book. My eye has always been drawn more indelibly to the Eyem, Kodoma District invasion and North Jade Dragon Fund collapse stories, causing me to all but completely overlook this gem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T17:51:05-08:00","id":23411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/21677-dragonblooded-breeding-and-the-scarlet-empress?p=21746#post21746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow. That's pretty mind blowingly stupid. I mean, the Exaltation is basically the most important thing, period, full stop, to the Dynasty. While I can certainly imagine a range of supersticions and prejudices around Aspect, lineage and breeding- especially amongst the patricians -I'd expect the the sages and savants of the Scarlet Dynasty to have a pretty good handle on most of what is and isn't BS in pure, practical terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is, and it isn't. The Sids main power is information, and they share that information incredibly sparingly, mostly because once you let it out, you can't control how it spreads. And up until very recently, it served their purpose to keep the DB in the dark as much as possible. After a thousand-odd years, it's kind of a tricky habit to break. Besides, it doesn't actually matter: it's just something they trot out to attack a house they want to attack anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T17:58:42-08:00","id":23414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/21677-dragonblooded-breeding-and-the-scarlet-empress?p=23411#post23411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is, and it isn't. The Sids main power is information, and they share that information incredibly sparingly, mostly because once you let it out, you can't control how it spreads. And up until very recently, it served their purpose to keep the DB in the dark as much as possible. After a thousand-odd years, it's kind of a tricky habit to break. Besides, it doesn't actually matter: it's just something they trot out to attack a house they want to attack anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>The DBs can track information correlating Aspect to strength of breeding and parents on their own. It's not like everything the Realm knows comes from the Sidereals, and the Sidereals just don't have <i>time</i> to run around stealing paperwork and research notes from every Dragon-blood who decides to, say, study <i>the single most important aspect of their society.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Once, there was a maiden... who spent all her time on the internet.<br /> &quot;Someone out there is WRONG,&quot; she said.<br /> So she tossed a noose made of golden light... and strangled her opponent.<br /> Both of them died alone.<br /> &quot;Love is for football players and cheerleaders,&quot; her obituary said.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","name":"notthepenguins","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"359"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T23:19:29-08:00","id":23559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notthepenguins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/21677-dragonblooded-breeding-and-the-scarlet-empress?p=23414#post23414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The DBs can track information correlating Aspect to strength of breeding and parents on their own. It's not like everything the Realm knows comes from the Sidereals, and the Sidereals just don't have <i>time</i> to run around stealing paperwork and research notes from every Dragon-blood who decides to, say, study <i>the single most important aspect of their society.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>And people never, ever maintain superstitions and ideas despite evidence to the contrary?<br /> <br /> Also, most DB have more important things to do, like maintaining the Realm, hunting Anathema, and...having orgies? I don't really know what DB do as a general rule, but I do know it's very important. Plus, who's going to do that paperwork? The Realm bureaucracy is busy enough managing the entire empire, and that assumes that there's some kind of systematic way to measure breeding strength, and you can reliably tell who has/will Exalt, which requires the Houses to be honest about one of their main strengths. Plus Exalting is, to a large extent, random: sure, breeding may may it more <i>likely</i> that someone will Exalt, but it's by no means any kind of systematic certainty. So, a few &quot;strong&quot; breeders could just have a bad statistical run, and some &quot;weak&quot; breeders could have a good run. Plus there's Lost Eggs to consider, and adoption...<br /> <br /> It's really complicated, is the point. They do try to keep track, but they're far from perfect. Hell, they don't even have printing, read the bit on how they handle updates to the law.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T10:40:05-08:00","id":23829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notthepenguins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/21677-dragonblooded-breeding-and-the-scarlet-empress?p=23414#post23414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The DBs can track information correlating Aspect to strength of breeding and parents on their own. It's not like everything the Realm knows comes from the Sidereals, and the Sidereals just don't have <i>time</i> to run around stealing paperwork and research notes from every Dragon-blood who decides to, say, study <i>the single most important aspect of their society.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the superstition is based off of them having an incomplete understanding of the mechanisms of terrestrial exaltation. They're going &quot;Look at that, with this generation's Dragonbloods almost exclusively married Earth Dragons, and a larger than average number of their kids Exalted, and most of them as Earth Dragons! That obviously means that purity of Aspect is a thing!&quot; While what actually is happening is &quot;Because this generation's dragonbloods married other dragonbloods almost exclusively, the exaltation rate of the next generation increased. Coincidentally, because a vast majority of the involved parents were Earth aspect, that higher proportion passed on to the next generation.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, in practice, it looks the same, IF they actually care about purity of aspect. But how did the whole superstition start? I would posit the Sids started it through the immaculate order, and then helped tilt the board in favor of those who did do so for a while, just enough that everyone had just enough doubt in their mind that &quot;Hey, they might actually have a thing going there....&quot; And I could definitely image the Sids starting this superstition, because if the Terrestrials are so focused on breeding with other Terrestrials of their Aspect, then they're actually breeding with other terrestrials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T12:05:47-08:00","id":23875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/21677-dragonblooded-breeding-and-the-scarlet-empress?p=23829#post23829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the superstition is based off of them having an incomplete understanding of the mechanisms of terrestrial exaltation. They're going &quot;Look at that, with this generation's Dragonbloods almost exclusively married Earth Dragons, and a larger than average number of their kids Exalted, and most of them as Earth Dragons! That obviously means that purity of Aspect is a thing!&quot; While what actually is happening is &quot;Because this generation's dragonbloods married other dragonbloods almost exclusively, the exaltation rate of the next generation increased. Coincidentally, because a vast majority of the involved parents were Earth aspect, that higher proportion passed on to the next generation.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, in practice, it looks the same, IF they actually care about purity of aspect. But how did the whole superstition start? I would posit the Sids started it through the immaculate order, and then helped tilt the board in favor of those who did do so for a while, just enough that everyone had just enough doubt in their mind that &quot;Hey, they might actually have a thing going there....&quot; And I could definitely image the Sids starting this superstition, because if the Terrestrials are so focused on breeding with other Terrestrials of their Aspect, then they're actually breeding with other terrestrials.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon-blooded - at least the ones who'd care to look into it - are <i>geniuses</i>. Saying &quot;they can't possibly figure it out because statistics are hard&quot; is... really, really dumb, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Once, there was a maiden... who spent all her time on the internet.<br /> &quot;Someone out there is WRONG,&quot; she said.<br /> So she tossed a noose made of golden light... and strangled her opponent.<br /> Both of them died alone.<br /> &quot;Love is for football players and cheerleaders,&quot; her obituary said.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","name":"notthepenguins","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"359"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T15:07:15-08:00","id":23997,"title":"","content":"Saying the Scarlet Dynasty has some erroneous suppositions and superstitions about things that help breeding and odds of Exaltation (including matter of Aspect inheritance) is fine. Saying that the Scarlet Dynasty has a measure of fairly meticulous and scientific knowledge to apply to their breeding practices is also fine. Saying that there are varying levels of either consideration across individuals, including those whom one might not expect, is to be expected.<br /> <br /> It's not so good to be <i>really specific</i> about this one purity of Aspect thing, ascribing it to virtually the entire Dynasty, <i>and</i> say that it's explicitly, objectively wrong, <i>and</i> say that the Sidereal Exalted <i>know</i> that it's wrong, and are deliberately withholding the information because it confers some unspecified advantage upon them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T15:20:19-08:00","id":24008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notthepenguins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/21677-dragonblooded-breeding-and-the-scarlet-empress?p=23875#post23875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon-blooded - at least the ones who'd care to look into it - are <i>geniuses</i>. Saying &quot;they can't possibly figure it out because statistics are hard&quot; is... really, really dumb, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not intending to say that they can't figure it out &quot;because statistics are hard&quot;. I'm saying that (1) Given natural variability in statistics, the difference in outcomes would be very small when people are actually attempting to breed for Aspect. (2) Humans tend to interpret data in a way that supports preconceived world views. There is nothing that indicates that Dragonbloods are any different. (3) &quot;Purity of Aspect&quot; is probably the dogma of the Immaculate Order.<br /> <br /> This would lead me to the conclusion that an overwhelming majority of the dragonbloods wouldn't question it when it looks to work, and the state religion says it works, the government says it works, so obviously it works. Even if someone subjects it to close scrutiny, given the immense levels of cultural religiousity in the Realm, the statistics would be close enough that it would probably be given the benefit of the doubt. <br /> <br /> I am by no means saying that a Dragonblood couldn't figure it out. I'm saying that it would be (1) unlikely, given the difficulty of calculating any individual's chances of exaltation, and then trying to find the formulae to make changes based off of minor breeding variations, and then applying that to a large enough observational pool to make it statistically viable? It would be the work of a lifetime. Even a Terrestrial lifetime. And it would have no guarantee of success. And (2) if someone did figure it out, what would happen? If it suits the Sidereal's needs to keep the data hushed-up, Chejop Kejak could use his already-established Resplendent Destiny as a high-level functionary in the imperial bureaucracy to find (fabricate) an ancient (just made) study that proves exactly what he wants. Given that the Mouth of Peace is also in Kejak's pocket, who would the Realm as a whole believe? Some random terrestrial that was probably viewed as an eccentric for investigating that in the first place? Or the head of the (very popular) state religion, who seems to have data backing them up from before the foundation of the Realm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}